1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,402
Today is September 28, 2026.

3
00:00:07,402 --> 00:00:15,331
Major US equity indices logged their first weekly gain in three weeks, but underlying market breadth severely deteriorated.

4
00:00:15,331 --> 00:00:22,782
The S and P five hundred, Nasdaq, and Dow advanced solely on heavy mega-cap artificial intelligence buying.

5
00:00:22,782 --> 00:00:26,030
Eight of eleven major sectors finished lower.

6
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:30,552
The equal-weighted S and P plunged roughly four percent over the week.

7
00:00:30,552 --> 00:00:35,197
For every advancing issue hitting new highs, ten hit fresh lows.

8
00:00:35,197 --> 00:00:39,621
Meanwhile, Treasury yields surged violently across the curve.

9
00:00:39,621 --> 00:00:46,716
Soft Treasury auction demand and persistent foreign selling drove the thirty-year yield above five point five percent.

10
00:00:46,716 --> 00:00:50,405
That marks its highest level since 2004.

11
00:00:50,405 --> 00:00:55,956
Fed fund futures now price a sixty-four percent probability of an October rate hike.

12
00:00:55,956 --> 00:00:59,743
A December follow-up hike sits at fifty-one percent.

13
00:00:59,743 --> 00:01:03,701
This sets up a direct clash between stocks and bonds.

14
00:01:03,701 --> 00:01:07,856
Equities are pricing long-term artificial intelligence growth.

15
00:01:07,856 --> 00:01:13,285
Fixed income is pricing persistent inflation and higher-for-longer borrowing costs.

16
00:01:13,285 --> 00:01:17,010
Both narratives cannot survive next week intact.

17
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:24,939
Markets face two primary macro catalysts: August core PCE on Friday and the September non-farm payrolls print.

18
00:01:24,939 --> 00:01:28,910
Core PCE is expected at three point three percent.

19
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:33,236
Non-farm payrolls are projected to slow to one hundred thousand.

20
00:01:33,236 --> 00:01:39,853
Unless labor data softens dramatically, hawkish rate momentum will crush equity valuation multiples.

21
00:01:39,853 --> 00:01:46,312
In commodities, West Texas Intermediate settled at ninety-two dollars and thirty-five cents per barrel.

22
00:01:46,312 --> 00:01:54,265
Geopolitical risk in the Strait of Hormuz remains an immediate volatility trigger following the rejection of temporary ceasefire terms.

23
00:01:54,265 --> 00:02:03,150
Turning to technology capital flows and supply chains, market liquidity remains intensely concentrated in high-end compute and data infrastructure.

24
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:05,748
Crucial tests loom this week.

25
00:02:05,748 --> 00:02:10,405
OpenAI hosts its annual developer conference in San Francisco.

26
00:02:10,405 --> 00:02:15,160
A new frontier model and cyber tools could reignite compute demand.

27
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:21,067
Washington will host a dedicated White House summit on artificial intelligence with key tech leaders.

28
00:02:21,067 --> 00:02:25,221
Export controls and government deployment take center stage.

29
00:02:25,221 --> 00:02:30,037
Meanwhile, Micron Technology reports fiscal fourth-quarter earnings.

30
00:02:30,037 --> 00:02:36,422
Guidance will directly validate or puncture memory pricing and AI data center capital expenditures.

31
00:02:36,422 --> 00:02:42,893
Looking at our primary individual equity drivers, three key names dictate trading momentum this week.

32
00:02:42,893 --> 00:02:45,148
First, Nvidia.

33
00:02:45,148 --> 00:02:47,084
Ticker N-V-D-A.

34
00:02:47,084 --> 00:02:53,260
Nvidia sits at the nexus of the macro rate fight and artificial intelligence infrastructure demand.

35
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:58,211
Fundamentally, enterprise Blackwell deployments remain supply-constrained.

36
00:02:58,211 --> 00:03:03,003
Hyperscaler capital expenditure revisions remain heavily skewed upward.

37
00:03:03,003 --> 00:03:06,630
Institutional positioning shows extreme crowding.

38
00:03:06,630 --> 00:03:11,618
The stock faces heavy technical resistance at the one hundred thirty dollar mark.

39
00:03:11,618 --> 00:03:15,932
Primary technical support holds at one hundred fifteen dollars.

40
00:03:15,932 --> 00:03:20,687
A break below one hundred fifteen risks systematic quant deleveraging.

41
00:03:20,687 --> 00:03:22,782
Next, Tesla.

42
00:03:22,782 --> 00:03:24,731
Ticker T-S-L-A.

43
00:03:24,731 --> 00:03:29,657
Tesla approaches its October first unveil of the next-generation Roadster.

44
00:03:29,657 --> 00:03:34,412
Market rumors point to SpaceX pneumatic cold-gas thruster integration.

45
00:03:34,412 --> 00:03:41,998
Fundamentally, automotive margins face relentless pressure from global price discounting and surging capital expenditures.

46
00:03:41,998 --> 00:03:46,655
Option positioning shows massive call skew ahead of October first.

47
00:03:46,655 --> 00:03:51,091
Strong technical resistance stands at two hundred sixty dollars.

48
00:03:51,091 --> 00:03:55,540
Crucial structural support sits firmly at two hundred twenty dollars.

49
00:03:55,540 --> 00:04:00,099
Failure to hold two hundred twenty opens downside toward two hundred.

50
00:04:00,099 --> 00:04:02,464
Finally, Alphabet.

51
00:04:02,464 --> 00:04:04,400
Ticker G-O-O-G-L.

52
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:10,748
Alphabet prepares for an orbital launch testing custom Tensor Processing Units in space this Thursday.

53
00:04:10,748 --> 00:04:16,508
This test marks a strategic move toward orbital artificial intelligence edge infrastructure.

54
00:04:16,508 --> 00:04:24,143
Institutional flows have rewarded Google for cost discipline and proprietary silicon autonomy against merchant accelerators.

55
00:04:24,248 --> 00:04:29,283
Technically, the stock faces resistance at one hundred eighty-five dollars.

56
00:04:29,233 --> 00:04:32,799
Support rests at one hundred seventy-two dollars.

57
00:04:32,799 --> 00:04:37,456
A break of one hundred seventy-two would signal broader tech distribution.

58
00:04:37,456 --> 00:04:42,015
Maintain strict risk limits across all high-beta tech exposure.

59
00:04:42,015 --> 00:04:46,023
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

60
00:04:46,023 --> 00:04:50,189
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
